  "id": "biological-age",
  "term": "biological age",
  "definition": "Biological age is an estimate of how far a person’s body has aged based on blood biomarkers that reflect overall physiological functioning, rather than simply the number of years since birth. It is used to capture differences between people in functional decline and molecular aging that chronological age may miss.",
